window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-8063f9ed486db057"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"manage-a-site\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">管理网站</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 末尾追加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>返回 ChatGPT 中的网站，可以查看流量、更改设置，或管理已保存的版本。</p> <p><a id=\"review-site-analytics\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">查看网站分析数据</h2> <p>Sites 会自动记录流量，无需分析 SDK。分析视图会显示独立访客总数和页面浏览量，以及这两项指标随时间的变化。你可以更改日期范围或时间粒度，以便比较不同时段。</p> <p>在 ChatGPT 桌面应用中打开 <strong>Sites</strong>，或在网页端前往 <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/sites\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT 中的 Sites（需联网）</a>。找到相应网站，然后选择 <strong>More actions（更多操作）</strong> &gt; <strong>Analytics（分析）</strong>。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：可交互的网站分析面板，显示七天内的独立访客数和页面浏览量。</p> </blockquote> <p>目前，非 Enterprise 工作区拥有的网站才可以使用分析功能。</p> <p><a id=\"change-a-site-url\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"url\">更改网站 URL</h2> <p>网站所有者可以在设置中管理网站名称和 URL。有关当前的控制选项和操作说明，请参阅帮助中心的<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001339-creating-and-using-chatgpt-sites\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">创建和使用 ChatGPT Sites（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"connect-a-custom-domain\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">连接自定义域名</h2> <p>如果所在地区支持自定义域名，你可以连接自己已拥有的根域名（apex domain）或子域名。Sites 不会替你注册域名，因此你必须能够更改该域名的 DNS 记录。</p> <p>目前，Enterprise 工作区尚不支持自定义域名。</p> <p>连接域名的步骤：</p> <ol> <li>打开网站设置并选择 <strong>Add domain（添加域名）</strong>。</li> <li>输入你想使用的根域名（apex domain）或子域名。</li> <li>复制 Sites 提供的 DNS 记录和值，然后通过你的域名服务商添加这些记录。</li> <li>等待几分钟，再返回网站设置并刷新域名状态。</li> </ol> <p>你也可以请 ChatGPT 帮你将域名指向网站。如果已启用浏览或电脑操作功能，ChatGPT 可以在你登录后协助你操作域名服务商的网站。</p> <p><a id=\"configure-runtime-environment-values\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">配置运行环境值</h2> <p>打开 <strong>Sites</strong>，再进入网站设置，即可添加、更新或移除托管环境变量和机密。不要把机密值放入提示词、附件或网站内容中。</p> <p>前往 <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/sites\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT 中的 Sites（需联网）</a>，找到相应网站，然后选择 <strong>More actions（更多操作）</strong> &gt; <strong>Settings（设置）</strong>。</p> <p>如果你正在处理本地源代码项目，也请遵循以下文件使用说明：</p> <p>不要将这些值保存在 <code>.openai/hosting.json</code> 中。确保本地 <code>.env</code> 和 <code>.env.example</code> 文件包含本地开发所需的键，并且不要提交机密值。</p> <p>请按照网站设置中显示的配置说明操作。有关当前所有者控制选项，请参阅帮助中心的<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001339-creating-and-using-chatgpt-sites\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">创建和使用 ChatGPT Sites（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"take-down-or-delete-a-site\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">下线或删除网站</h2> <p>如果想移除访问权限但保留网站，请打开共享设置，将访问范围限制为自己或选定的人员。确认之前的受众已无法打开该网站。</p> <p>要永久删除网站：</p> <ol> <li>打开 <strong>Sites</strong> 并找到相应网站。</li> <li>选择 <strong>Delete site（删除网站）</strong>，并按提示操作。</li> <li>输入网站的 slug，然后选择 <strong>Permanently delete（永久删除）</strong>。</li> </ol> <p>删除网站会将其永久移除，无法恢复。</p> <p><a id=\"understand-projects-versions-and-deployments\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">了解项目、版本和部署</h2> <p>对于现有本地项目，请让 Sites 检查兼容性，并为发布做好准备。</p> <p>网站会继续保留在 ChatGPT 的 <strong>Sites</strong> 中，你可以重新打开、调整、配置和分享它。</p> <p>对于本地源代码项目，Sites 项目会将源代码与由 Sites 管理的托管服务关联起来。Sites 会在 <code>.openai/hosting.json</code> 中保存这种关联以及可选的存储绑定名称。新建的本地起始项目可以暂时没有 <code>project_id</code>；Sites 在创建托管项目后会添加该字段。</p> <p>例如，一个已创建托管项目、使用关系型数据库绑定且不使用文件存储的网站，其配置可以是：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-json\">{\n  \"project_id\": \"&lt;project-id&gt;\",\n  \"d1\": \"DB\",\n  \"r2\": null\n}\n</code></pre> <p>即使创建网站的 ChatGPT Work 对话结束，网站仍会显示在你的 Sites 列表中。你不需要本地项目或清单文件，也可以直接在网页端开始创建网站。网站与 ChatGPT Project 是彼此独立的。</p> <p>Sites 发布分为两个不同阶段：</p> <ol> <li><strong>保存版本。</strong> ChatGPT 会构建一个可部署的版本。对于本地源代码项目，ChatGPT 会将该版本与构建时使用的 Git commit 关联起来。如果你想先审核候选部署版本，请使用此阶段。</li> <li><strong>部署版本。</strong> ChatGPT 会发布已保存的版本，并在部署成功后提供生产环境 URL。只有在你确实打算让选定受众访问网站时，才使用此阶段。</li> </ol> <p>如果需要识别之前的部署候选版本，可以请 ChatGPT 列出或检查已保存的版本。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"manage-a-site\">Manage a site</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Return to your site in ChatGPT to review its traffic, change its settings, or manage its saved versions.</p> <h2 id=\"review-site-analytics\">Review site analytics</h2> <p>Sites records traffic automatically, without an analytics SDK. The analytics view shows total unique visitors and page views, plus both metrics over time. Change the date range or granularity to compare periods.</p> <p>Open <strong>sites</strong> in the ChatGPT desktop app, or go to <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/sites\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">sites in ChatGPT (online)</a> on the web. Find the site, then select <strong>More actions</strong> &gt; <strong>Analytics</strong>.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: Interactive sites analytics dashboard showing unique visitors and page views over seven days.</p> </blockquote> <p>Analytics is currently available for sites that aren't owned by an Enterprise workspace.</p> <h2 id=\"change-a-site-url\">Change a site URL</h2> <p>Site owners can manage the site's name and URL in its settings. For the current controls and instructions, see <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001339-creating-and-using-chatgpt-sites\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Creating and using ChatGPT Sites (online)</a> in the Help Center.</p> <h2 id=\"connect-a-custom-domain\">Connect a custom domain</h2> <p>Where custom domains are available, you can connect an apex domain or subdomain that you already own. Sites doesn't register domains for you, so you must be able to change the domain's DNS records.</p> <p>Custom domains aren't available in Enterprise workspaces at launch.</p> <p>To connect a domain:</p> <ol> <li>Open the site's settings and select <strong>Add domain</strong>.</li> <li>Enter the apex domain or subdomain you want to use.</li> <li>Copy the DNS records and values sites provides, then add them through your domain provider.</li> <li>Wait a few minutes, then return to the site's settings and refresh the domain status.</li> </ol> <p>You can also ask ChatGPT to help point the domain at your site. If browsing or computer use is enabled, ChatGPT can help you navigate your domain provider after you sign in.</p> <h2 id=\"configure-runtime-environment-values\">Configure runtime environment values</h2> <p>Open <strong>sites</strong>, then open the site's settings to add, update, or remove hosted environment variables and secrets. Keep secret values out of prompts, attached files, and site content.</p> <p>Go to <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/sites\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">sites in ChatGPT (online)</a>, find the site, then select <strong>More actions</strong> &gt; <strong>Settings</strong>.</p> <p>If you're working with a local source project, also follow this file guidance:</p> <p>Don't store these values in <code>.openai/hosting.json</code>. Keep local <code>.env</code> and <code>.env.example</code> files aligned with the keys needed for local development, and don't commit secret values.</p> <p>Follow the configuration instructions shown in the site's settings. For current owner controls, see <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001339-creating-and-using-chatgpt-sites\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Creating and using ChatGPT Sites (online)</a> in the Help Center.</p> <h2 id=\"take-down-or-delete-a-site\">Take down or delete a site</h2> <p>To remove access without deleting a site, open its sharing settings and restrict access to yourself or selected people. Confirm that the previous audience can no longer open it.</p> <p>To permanently delete a site:</p> <ol> <li>Open <strong>sites</strong> and locate the site.</li> <li>Select <strong>Delete site</strong> and follow the instructions in the prompt.</li> <li>Enter the site slug, then select <strong>Permanently delete</strong>.</li> </ol> <p>Deleting a site permanently removes it. You can't restore a deleted site.</p> <h2 id=\"understand-projects-versions-and-deployments\">Understand projects, versions, and deployments</h2> <p>For an existing local project, ask sites to check compatibility and prepare it for publishing.</p> <p>A site stays available in <strong>sites</strong> in ChatGPT, where you can reopen, refine, configure, and share it.</p> <p>For a local source project, a sites project links your source to hosting managed through sites. Sites stores that linkage and optional storage binding names in <code>.openai/hosting.json</code>. A newly created local starter can begin without a <code>project_id</code>; sites adds one after it provisions the hosted project.</p> <p>For example, a provisioned site that uses a relational database binding and no file storage can contain:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-json\">{\n  \"project_id\": \"&lt;project-id&gt;\",\n  \"d1\": \"DB\",\n  \"r2\": null\n}\n</code></pre> <p>A site appears in your sites list even after the ChatGPT Work chat that created it ends. You don't need a local project or manifest to start a site on the web. A site is separate from a ChatGPT Project.</p> <p>Sites publishing has two separate stages:</p> <ol> <li><strong>Save a version.</strong> ChatGPT builds a deployable version. For a local source project, ChatGPT associates the version with the Git commit used for the build. Use this stage when you want a reviewable deployment candidate.</li> <li><strong>Deploy a version.</strong> ChatGPT publishes a saved version and reports the production URL when deployment succeeds. Use this only when you intend for the selected audience to access the site.</li> </ol> <p>Ask ChatGPT to list or inspect saved versions when you need to identify a previous deployment candidate.</p>"};
